{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>You shall bring out all the tithe</b> etc. In three years you bring out all the tithes. How so? In the first year of the septennial cycle, first tithe to the Levite, second tithe to eat by the householder in Jerusalem — and likewise in the second year. And in the third year, first tithe to the Levite and the poor man's tithe to distribute to the poor. As we derive from 'the third year, the year of the tithe' — a year in which there is only one of the two tithes, and this is the first tithe; but in any case one must give the poor man's tithe in place of the second tithe. Thus at the end of three years you have brought out all the tithes that you have to bring out: first tithe, second tithe, poor man's tithe." "<b>And you shall set down within your gates.</b> Regarding second tithe I told you to bring it up to Jerusalem; but regarding the poor man's tithe — <b>and you shall set it down within your gates.</b>"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:52.824242322Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}